// js/poeItemIcons.js (v8)  [ASCII build - safe for any file encoding]
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Official PoE art on equipment tiles, with NO synchronous work inside DOM
// mutation callbacks.
//
// The remaining [Violation] cause in v7 - my own bug:
//   MutationObserver callbacks are MICROTASKS: they run inside whichever task
//   changed the DOM. During auto battle that is gameConfigSpeed.js's timer.
//   v7 still ran the heavy pass SYNCHRONOUSLY from the callback whenever the
//   throttle window had elapsed:
//       if (since >= THROTTLE) { runPass(); return; }   // inside that tick
//   so every ~400ms the game's own tick paid 40-60ms and Chrome reported it
//   against gameConfigSpeed.js lines 64 / 119.
//
// v8 rules:
//   1. the observer callback ONLY sets a flag and schedules a timer. It never
//      queries the DOM, never measures, never decorates.
//   2. the pass runs in its own task (setTimeout 0), scoped to cached roots
//      instead of the whole document.
//   3. observers are attached per root, plus a body observer with
//      subtree:false that only catches modal open/close.
//   4. a pass is skipped entirely while the tab is hidden.
