/* --- poeUiFix.js --- */
// js/poeUiFix.js (v8)  [ASCII build - safe for any file encoding]
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 1. the stat panel stays gone: the panel, its button, its stylesheet and any
//    leftover block older versions appended into the character panel
// 2. hides the toolbar currency-stash button (kept from the earlier request)
// 3. official PoE art on the ten sidebar equipment rows, with NO emoji flash
// 4. the left equipment column becomes ONE item per row and the item names wrap
//    instead of being clipped. Root cause: .bagov-eq is 1fr 1fr, and 1fr means
//    minmax(auto,1fr) whose min is min-content - a name with white-space:nowrap
//    therefore widened its own grid column and pushed the row out of the panel.
//    Fix: minmax(0,1fr) + allow the name to wrap.
// 5. the "currency / back to bag" tabs under the stash title are hidden. The
//    back button in the modal header (.bagov-headbtns) is NOT touched.
// 6. the craft-target box (.bagov-tgtbox) and the bag-craftable list are moved
//    out of the left column to directly under the currency grid (.bagov-sgrid)
//    inside .bagov-right, so they inherit the same width as the grid.
//
// why icons used to flash: the game rebuilds #sidebar-equip-summary on every
// refresh and earlier versions re-decorated from a throttled timer, so a rebuilt
// row kept its emoji until that timer fired. Three guards remove the window:
//   a) renderer hook - any HY function whose source mentions sidebar-equip is
//      wrapped, so decoration runs inside the call that rendered the rows
//   b) microtask observer on the rows container and on its parent, so a whole
//      element replacement is caught and the observer rebound at once
